{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans","id":707979,"title":"Question about Demons and Prometheans ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-18T19:02:45-07:00","id":707979,"title":"Question about Demons and Prometheans ?","content":"I wanted to know does that thing that makes humans hate Prometheans work on demons ? <br /> <br /> If not I was wondering if maybe agents of the god-machine could use Prometheans to detect a demons by seeing who does not react badly to them ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T19:27:58-07:00","id":708037,"title":"","content":"Pending any possible change in second edition Promethean, the Disquiet already affects most supernatural beings exactly or nearly the same as mortal humans, so there's not even any loophole to exploit with spoofing. I'd say the Unchained have no special immunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T19:30:01-07:00","id":708041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=708037#post708037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pending any possible change in second edition Promethean, the Disquiet already affects most supernatural beings exactly or nearly the same as mortal humans, so there's not even any loophole to exploit with spoofing. I'd say the Unchained have no special immunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for other Prometheans. They don't Disquiet each other. So, could you spoof that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T19:57:16-07:00","id":708070,"title":"","content":"Well I thought the reason it affected people and supernaturals was because they are part of the world. I was thinking demons would be immune because they have no place in the world they have to make there own place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T02:25:57-07:00","id":708441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans#post707979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to know does that thing that makes humans hate Prometheans work on demons ?<br /> <br /> If not I was wondering if maybe agents of the god-machine could use Prometheans to detect a demons by seeing who does not react badly to them ?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans#post707979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to know does that thing that makes humans hate Prometheans work on demons ?<br /> <br /> If not I was wondering if maybe agents of the god-machine could use Prometheans to detect a demons by seeing who does not react badly to them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Stupid Loserman says, Demons by default have no special immunity or vulnerability called out in the text, so it's really a matter of how the ST rules Disquiet effects supernaturals. For my money, even if your assumption is that Disquiet works because it's all based on mortals and other supernaturals being &quot;natural&quot;, then I would say that demons -aren't- exempt because the God-Machine and its workings are so heavily ingrained in the basic nature of the universe that you could argue they are the -most- natural supernatural things.<br /> <br /> So, here's what would happen, in my game. If Disquiet worked on Supernaturals, then it would affect a Demon as normal. Crucially, while the demon would definitely feel it, he would choose how to express such feelings - he is the full master of the normal tics and physical behaviors that belie emotion, remember?<br /> <br /> So. Given that a)prometheans are extremely rare, b)the agents of the God-Machine don't necessarily know what Disquiet is or how it works, c)the agents of the God-Machine that aren't angels aren't necessarily immune to it either and d)you couldn't predict how any given demon would react to it -anyways-, I don't see it being a plan that the God-Machine attempts, or at least not more than a few trial runs.<br /> <br /> But again, that's what -I- would do. Do what you want in your own chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=708041#post708041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for other Prometheans. They don't Disquiet each other. So, could you spoof that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoofing doesn't change anything about how a Demon reacts to any stimuli, unless that stimuli would very specifically out it as being nonhuman. That's all Spoofing does, is to help a Demon pass as human. So, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T03:05:35-07:00","id":708468,"title":"","content":"While we don't know what will change in second edition, there's a first edition promethean book that discusses the issue of disquiet and other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Although it sounds like disquiet will be less of an issue if a promethean is fulfilling their role, but time will tell.<br /> <br /> One, in the ST can just rule that other supernaturals are immune to disquiet.<br /> <br /> Two, if they aren't immune, then they can appropriate supernatural effects to mitigate the effects. For example, a demon might have an embed or exploit or a near effect gadget to deal with it. Perhaps something based on Cool Heads Prevail or Associate and Integrate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:51:45-07:00","id":708696,"title":"","content":"One of the demon splats mentions Prometheans in the stereotypes - the demon in question studied under one for a while, before killing them - and still doesn't know why they did that last part. I would interpret that as normal-functioning Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T21:56:29-07:00","id":709954,"title":"","content":"Pending any changes in 2nd/Firestorm Chronicle edition, I've ruled that Disquiet effects the Covers as normal, but not the Demon. Acting against the Disquiet Conditions* counts as a compromise. So if you are willing to reveal multiple Covers, suffer compromise or hang about in demonic form then you can hang with the Created.<br /> <br /> I thought it was more interesting than just saying it effects them the same even if it is practically the same. I should add that I had no plan to inform the players, they would discover this during play. But the game was cancelled before the first session, so I have no idea how it would work out in play.<br /> <br /> *Planned on using the write up in Mortal Remains, tweaked with the Prommie books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T22:08:32-07:00","id":709962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=708696#post708696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the demon splats mentions Prometheans in the stereotypes - the demon in question studied under one for a while, before killing them - and still doesn't know why they did that last part. I would interpret that as normal-functioning Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Disquiet tends to have a leadup and the stereotype blurb in question is from the <i>Integrators</i>, I'd say that's a stronger implication of something else at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:01:57-07:00","id":718728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=709962#post709962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Disquiet tends to have a leadup and the stereotype blurb in question is from the <i>Integrators</i>, I'd say that's a stronger implication of something else at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubtful. Given it would be a new unique effect, it's more likely to be normal Disquiet compounded by demonic paranoia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:22:03-07:00","id":718755,"title":"","content":"Or, just as likely, we have two different writers with two different takes on the issue, and no one forcing them to adhere to the same take. This is a crossover issue, and like most crossover issues, should be firmly under the venue of individual STs and the needs of their individual stories. Does it make sense for the Unchained to be immune to Disquiet? Are the Principle and God-Machine related in some way?<br /> <br /> <br /> In either case, I generally consider that the Unchained -should- be immune to Disquiet; demons have the power to try and hide out as another supernatural through the use of non-soul pacts, Show of Power, and Deep Cover (I think that's the one that lets you spoof as another supernatural). It doesn't make sense for a demon that's pretending to be a Prommie to be hit with Disquiet. And if that demon had several human Covers, each of which has encountered the prommie? Each should be suffering from different levels of Disquiet, not a consistant one across all layers, and the demon should act out each as appropriate - it would be strange enough to attract God Machine attention. <br /> <br /> So, IMHO, Unchained should be immune as a whole, but need to <b><i>act</i></b> like he suffered from it as appropriate, or get hit with a Compromise check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:55:09-07:00","id":718857,"title":"","content":"Isn't the God-Machine the most natural of the supernaturals?<br /> <br /> Aren't Prometheans the less natural of them all?<br /> <br /> Shouldn't Demons &amp; Angels shudder and twitch whenever they encounter a Promethean? I mean, they're <i>more than glitches.</i> They are terribly more than glitches; glitches are bugs, loopholes, problems, etc... Prometheans not Mario-turning-blue-because-you-jumped-inside-a-wall weird, they're more like a hand pressing against the static of your television and breaking the screen. It should not be happening.<br /> <br /> My two cents, of course. As MCN and many others said, it's up to the ST to decide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:07:00-07:00","id":718896,"title":"","content":"I think I'm on Magnum's side for this one. Also, for some reason, I like the Unchained to be the &quot;punching bag&quot; splat. Does that make sense? I'm glad that the Begotten and the Unchained have such difficulties interacting, for example. I think I want them to face the same challenges that everybody else faces, plus their own, and their powers are designed for the Unchained to figure out how to deal with them rather than straight-up dismissing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:24:23-07:00","id":721731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=718728#post718728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doubtful. Given it would be a new unique effect, it's more likely to be normal Disquiet compounded by demonic paranoia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal Disquiet is not subtle enough to manage &quot;I killed it and I don't know why&quot; and the God-Machine is well-established in its ability to make sleeper agents.<br /> <br /> The metaphysical pedigree of the Unchained has precedent in the form of the other two primary ephemeral beings re: immunity to Disquiet and nothing about the Fall suggests they should gain a vulnerability to the freakish hateful magnetism of Azoth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=718755#post718755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, IMHO, Unchained should be immune as a whole, but need to <b><i>act</i></b> like he suffered from it as appropriate, or get hit with a Compromise check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go so far as a necessitating a check, seeing as even speaking languages or demonstrating skills &quot;you&quot; don't possess aren't checks on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=718857#post718857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the God-Machine the most natural of the supernaturals?<br /> <br /> Aren't Prometheans the less natural of them all?</div> </div> </div> </div>No and no.<br /> <br /> The Machine is the most integrated into human society by virtue of how it operates, but the necessary weirdness behind Infrastructure should make it abundantly clear that God is only &quot;natural&quot; in the sense that It has not evinced any real extramaterial origin. The Divine Fire shares the same headspace of &quot;simultaneously natural and supernatural and the Created are strange and unsettling chiefly due to the matter of how <i>concentrated</i> their chunk of the force is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T03:36:26-07:00","id":722502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=721731#post721731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go so far as a necessitating a check, seeing as even speaking languages or demonstrating skills &quot;you&quot; don't possess aren't checks on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div> actually, you do suffer Compromise checks for displaying knowledge that your Cover shouldn't have, at least in front of witnesses. That is the whole raison d'etre behind the fourth specialty you gain at character creation, after all. <br /> <br /> There absolutely should be discretion involved on a case by case basis, I'm not advocating a hard line approach. But I am of the opinion that demon should act like a regular mortal faced with the supernatural, even if he shrugs off the effect. This is a game where you play an undercover spy, after all, playing a part. YMMV.<br /> <br /> <br /> BIgDamnHero, no, I don't get what you mean by punching bag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-24-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T08:44:17-07:00","id":723179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=722502#post722502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BIgDamnHero, no, I don't get what you mean by punching bag.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this idea in my head that the Unchained are the ultimate underdogs of the WoD (perhaps not as much as Prometheans, but close). They get a lot to work with, certainly, but their interactions with the world should always have them at a disadvantage. They adopt human identities, and are thus vulnerable to the things humans are.<br /> <br /> Actually, that last sentence is a much better summary of what I think about the Unchained. &quot;If you want to pretend to be human, you have to put up with the same issues as a human.&quot;<br /> <br /> Granted, Satchel makes some very good points (as he normally does) about why the Unchained should be immune to Disquiet from a Watsonian perspective, and it has me reconsidering my stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T12:53:26-07:00","id":724025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=723179#post723179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have this idea in my head that the Unchained are the ultimate underdogs of the WoD (perhaps not as much as Prometheans, but close). They get a lot to work with, certainly, but their interactions with the world should always have them at a disadvantage. They adopt human identities, and are thus vulnerable to the things humans are.<br /> <br /> Actually, that last sentence is a much better summary of what I think about the Unchained. &quot;If you want to pretend to be human, you have to put up with the same issues as a human.&quot;<br /> <br /> Granted, Satchel makes some very good points (as he normally does) about why the Unchained should be immune to Disquiet from a Watsonian perspective, and it has me reconsidering my stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Put it that way, and it makes me think, they are immune to Disquiet, in their Demonic Form. Being in a Human cover, they suffer Disquiet (I suppose you could let them refuse to roll at the cost of a compromise). If they somehow acquired a Cover that is immune to Disquiet (Maybe an Ephemeral Cover crafted from a beast's Horror?), they could probably skim around that. Or maybe they could patch in the immunity from a Scion (the child of a Promethean, that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T05:52:14-07:00","id":725679,"title":"","content":"How is that functionally different than &quot;they are immune to Disquiet, but may have to act the part or face Compromise&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T06:13:49-07:00","id":725753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=721731#post721731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal Disquiet is not subtle enough to manage &quot;I killed it and I don't know why&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Read Asylum. One of the cases mentioned is the aftermath of a Disquiet-inspired killing, and as the Disquiet faded in the dead Promethean's absence, the killers couldn't understand why they'd acted that way.<br /> <br /> And the stereotypes section is a bizarre place to include a sleeper agent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:44:09-07:00","id":726759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=725753#post725753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read Asylum. One of the cases mentioned is the aftermath of a Disquiet-inspired killing, and as the Disquiet faded in the dead Promethean's absence, the killers couldn't understand why they'd acted that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, in fact, read Asylum, probably far more recently than you. You're describing the lesser-affected supporters of a murderer ceasing to provide an alibi in the <i>option</i> for that case where the victim was a Promethean rather than a demon or an unfortunate homeless woman. Bennings himself is only unsure why he went <i>as far as</i> murdering Jane Doe and still demonstrates the a similar obsession to the one he had before.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the section on Disquiet in the Appendix doesn't say &quot;no reason&quot; \u2014 it says &quot;spurious or downright false reasons,&quot; which are kind of outside the realm of forgetting for a being with perfect recall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the stereotypes section is a bizarre place to include a sleeper agent. </div> </div> </div>For the faction mechanically and narratively incentivized to hang out around angels and engage in regular low-level mole behavior? Not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T06:37:23-07:00","id":728658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=725679#post725679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that functionally different than &quot;they are immune to Disquiet, but may have to act the part or face Compromise&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> Disquiet is likely going to function through Conditions, while my way was going to function on a &quot;draw down angels to kill you&quot; method. So, the punishment will be different for violating will be different. If you go along with it? Not much at all. Honestly, both are good ways of modeling it, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T08:27:03-07:00","id":729017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=726759#post726759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bennings himself is only unsure why he went <i>as far as</i> murdering Jane Doe and still demonstrates the a similar obsession to the one he had before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we disagree on the spectrum of meanings covered by &quot;not knowing why.&quot; I'm assuming that the obsession in question, for the demon, was paranoia, because demons are always paranoid, and paranoia is never not going to be stoked by Disquiet, but after the fact, that can easily leave the demon unclear on why it felt so paranoid it needed to kill the Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the faction mechanically and narratively incentivized to hang out around angels and engage in regular low-level mole behavior? Not really. </div> </div> </div>You said sleeper agents, and Integrators are the worst possible faction to use as sleeper agents. But if you really want to insist that the section suggesting how typical encounters between demons and other supernaturals might go is likely to refer to something as specific and edge-case as the God-Machine cunningly embedding a sleeper agent in the faction most likely to be shunned, distrusted, and killed by other demons, and then activating it to kill a Promethean in a manner highly resembling Disquiet, for no discernible reason (and that the God-Machine has its agents kill Prometheans often enough to merit them being the extra supernatural chosen for the Integrators), then I suppose I can't stop you. But it's more likely that the section is referring to a Promethean, because Integrators are a likely faction to be interested in Prometheans (another approach to divinity; they don't just want to surrender, remember), followed by the sequence above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T09:54:56-07:00","id":729193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=729017#post729017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said sleeper agents, and Integrators are the worst possible faction to use as sleeper agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>For actions targeted at other demons who know the character is an Integrator and are not Integrators themselves? Sure.<br /> <br /> For actions targeted at those specific frequently-more-trusting demons and the world at large? Nah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if you really want to insist that the section suggesting how typical encounters between demons and other supernaturals might go </div> </div> </div>The Agendas are broad, broad categories, the viewpoint characters for the stereotypes are single entities, and the Integrators are the most explicitly subfactionalized in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is likely to refer to something as specific and edge-case as the God-Machine cunningly embedding a sleeper agent in the faction most likely to be shunned, distrusted, and killed by other demons, and then activating it to kill a Promethean </div> </div> </div>&quot;One of the greatest sources of strife and insecurity for the Unchained&quot; being applied to the subversion of a member of the faction most likely to engage with the Machine on a non-hostile level.<br /> <br /> In a fashion that either deliberately or accidentally results in the death of a character whose &quot;patron's&quot; supernatural qualities bear a number of similarities to the Machine after a period of the latter tutoring the former.<br /> <br /> Leaving the demon with knowledge no other demon can now possess without consulting a perfect liar and the Promethean either dead (and thus unable to complete the Pilgrimage), mortal, or still on the Pilgrimage with a major milestone completed and/or one less free resurrection on their hands, depending on type.<br /> <br /> &quot;Edge-case.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in a manner highly resembling Disquiet, </div> </div> </div>Your metric for this has literally been expressed solely as &quot;they don't know why they killed them and they were a Promethean.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mages stereotype directly above it has the viewpoint character lamenting the fact that a mage was killed <i>before</i> they could learn anything from them and the Vampires stereotype is literally just &quot;They have nothing to offer us.&quot; This is a blatantly ruthless individual with a pattern of evaluating others by their position and utility to them and a clear lack of concern for murder as an action in itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> for no discernible reason </div> </div> </div>That recurring theory that the Fall is a designed part of angelic existence combined with the common fact of Integrators wanting to rejoin the System on their own terms or to alter its nature would seem an ample explanation for why the God-Machine might manipulate circumstances to alter what a given Idealist's own terms translate to or prevent a change to its nature from being reverse-engineered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (and that the God-Machine has its agents kill Prometheans often enough to merit them being the extra supernatural chosen for the Integrators), </div> </div> </div>You are reaching for a meaning I did not imply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:17:59-07:00","id":739436,"title":"","content":"My initial thought is that Disquiet is too integral to the core of the splat to let a supernatural template completely ignore it.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly like the &quot;A demon must behave as if he had Disquiet or risk compromise&quot; solution either. Compromise is based on behaving as what observers see as out of character. At least the first two stages of Disquiet strike me as too internal to have anyone think you're acting grossly out of character and I'm not convinced that not showing the requisite amount of unease and frustration that the third stage requires would either.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, the effect of a Promethean on demons should serve the needs of your story and the storyteller should make that call based on those needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:26:23-07:00","id":739642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IceIX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=739436#post739436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial thought is that Disquiet is too integral to the core of the splat to let a supernatural template completely ignore it. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>It's plausible, though. According to the beta test version of <b>Beast</b> (which went out to backers yesterday), Beasts are immune to Disquiet. The Dark Mother loves all her Children, even the adopted ones, and wants them to be a Family<br /> <br /> (Of course, other supernaturals still have problems with Disquiet, even if there's a Beast mediating. But then, what family <i>doesn't</i> have a few issues, and the occasional &quot;quirky&quot; relative? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-29-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T07:47:55-07:00","id":741744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=739642#post739642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's plausible, though. According to the beta test version of <b>Beast</b> (which went out to backers yesterday), Beasts are immune to Disquiet. The Dark Mother loves all her Children, even the adopted ones, and wants them to be a Family<br /> <br /> (Of course, other supernaturals still have problems with Disquiet, even if there's a Beast mediating. But then, what family <i>doesn't</i> have a few issues, and the occasional &quot;quirky&quot; relative? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>The downside, of course, is that the only creatures that can tolerate your presence are monstrous nightmare abusers, which should worry you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That Beasts are the exception here makes me happy in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:12:26-07:00","id":742276,"title":"","content":"Ugh, I was hoping that Promethean 2nd was going to fix the Disquiet issue. Guess I'll have to house-rule hack it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:29:25-07:00","id":742341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=742276#post742276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, I was hoping that Promethean 2nd was going to fix the Disquiet issue. Guess I'll have to house-rule hack it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it's really a huge deal to have to say, &quot;This one (or more) splat(s) is/are immune to Disquiet.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really get why so many people are against supernaturals being affected by Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T12:29:29-07:00","id":742490,"title":"","content":"Cross-over, mostly, I think. It's hard when you are obligated to kill your team-mate due to supernatural hate-plague.<br /> <br /> As far as Demons, specifically: they are kind-of a special case. Their Primum leads to the interpretation that they are somewhat self-contained, yet they are still part of reality. Their mastery over their Cover and general alien nature can be construed as not being as sensitive to the imposed feelings of Disquiet, but they also feel what their Covers (which are &quot;human&quot;) feel. The whole relationship between G-M Angels (and thus, tangently, Demons) and Quashmallim makes things confusing (because the relationship, if any, is not defined, though hinted at).<br /> <br /> Note that Ghosts and Spirits are explicitly immune to Disquiet (in 1ed). Angels are ephemerals, too, and might also be immune. Demons may or may not inherit the immunity, despite no longer being ephemeral.<br /> <br /> Note also that Vampires and Werewolves don't react to Disquiet the same as humans (and near-humans, such as Mages, and presumably Sin-Eaters): All they suffer from is penalties to control their &quot;rage&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-30-2015, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:31:25-07:00","id":742893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/707979-question-about-demons-and-prometheans?p=742341#post742341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, it's really a huge deal to have to say, &quot;This one (or more) splat(s) is/are immune to Disquiet.&quot; <br /> I don't really get why so many people are against supernaturals being affected by Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because it makes Promethean's difficult to cross-over without some house-rule hacking. And honestly, Promethean is so difficult to play as it is that I'm hoping for some major revisions and/or nerfing of both Wastelands and Disquiet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:23:57-08:00","id":759346,"title":"","content":"There's a promethean book that gives &quot;Make all supernaturals immune to disquiet&quot; an available option, and &quot;here are ways that the various splats could counteract disquiet with their native abilities if you do decide to leave them vulnerable to it.&quot; <br /> <br /> Such things as using cool heads prevail or call out to stop a pitchfork and torch welding mob.<br /> <br /> Or use miles away to resist disquiet. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}